d 'ESREG': module to estimate the endogenous switching regression with heterogeneous selection on gains
d
d  esreg estimates the endogenous switching regression (the Roy
d model with two regimes): a probit selection equation and an
d outcome equation for each regime, by full-information maximum
d likelihood or by a two-step estimator whose variance is that of
d the whole procedure (stacked moments). It reports the treatment
d effects ATT, ATU and ATE and the selection on gains, kappa = rho1
d sigma1 - rho0 sigma0, constant or heterogeneous in the covariates
d (kappa(x)), with standard errors from the influence functions of
d the whole procedure (the estimation of the parameters, the
d averaging over the units and their covariance), by observation,
d by cluster or through the survey design (svyset: the svy prefix
d for the likelihood, vce(svy) for the two-step). An augmented
d two-step adds Hermite terms, in both regimes or in one, when the
d conditional mean of the regime errors is not linear. A family of
d post-estimation commands checks the assumptions one by one:
d esrdiag (strength, variation and support of the selection
d equation), esrtest (specification of the index, sufficiency of
d the instruments, constant kappa, normality by regime, and a
d pseudo-difference-in-differences on the index), esrcurve (the
d effect by quantile group of the score), esrmte (the marginal
d treatment effect, parametric and semiparametric) and esrreport (a
d reading of the results and the route to report). A dialog box and
d help examples run from clickable links are included. The commands
d are validated against etregress, movestay, msat and a Python
d reference implementation, and their standard errors against
d brute-force influence functions. A technical note documents the
d model, the tests and the estimators; it is included as an
d ancillary file (esreg_technical_note.pdf). 
d
d KW: endogenous switching regression
d KW: Roy model
d KW: treatment effects
d KW: selection on gains
d KW: marginal treatment effect
d KW: control function
d KW: survey design
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261005
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar,  Universite Laval 
d Support: email aabd@@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
